Wound Planimetry command-line tool (@neurodesk/wound-planimetry)
================================================================

This package is MIT-licensed (LICENSE). It implements calibrated digital wound
planimetry and heuristic color-based Red-Yellow-Black (RYB) tissue estimation
in pure JavaScript:

- Otsu thresholding for automatic wound-bed segmentation (Otsu, IEEE TSMC 1979)
- Kundin ellipsoid wound-area approximation (Thomas & Wysocki, Ostomy Wound Manage 1990)
- Color-based Red (granulation), Yellow (slough/fibrin), Black (eschar/necrosis)
  tissue estimation in CIE L*a*b* and HSV space (Mukherjee et al., BioMed Res Int 2014)

Research and educational software — heuristic color-based RYB estimates are not a
trained clinical classifier or medical device.
